Subject: [PATCH 7/9] docs: correct deployment, CI, plugin and install facts

- README and CONTRIBUTING told contributors to run `uv sync`. The root
  pyproject.toml only holds tool configuration, so `uv sync` creates an empty
  virtual environment and `make test` then fails with "No module named pytest".
  Use `make install`, which is what the Makefile actually provides, and stop
  listing uv as a requirement.
- README: list all 10 plugins, describe deploy/ accurately and add a container
  deployment section.
- module-mapping: the gateway has 33 Go files (17 tests), reads its upstream
  from GATEWAY_UPSTREAM_URL rather than FORGEMESH_UPSTREAM, CI has four jobs,
  and the deployment section now describes runnable artifacts. Deviation D2
  (missing Dockerfile) is resolved and removed from section 4, as the
  document's maintenance rules require.
- CHANGELOG: record the images, compose, Kubernetes, CI and test changes of
  this series.
